                        "review": "Edit: I have a lot more hours in the game than the current playtime suggests.\n\nI can't explain it but I keep coming back to this year after year for a few hours every now and then. It's not the kinda game you sit and play for 8 hours straight on a Saturday but there's some factor I can't put my finger on that makes it sneak up in the back of your brain after a few months and make you want to hear the music again, see what kind of run you can put together, and what kind of shenanigans you might get yourself into depriving the locals of their holy artifacts.\n\nI'm sure other reviews will go into great detail about WHY the game is good - and I think every part of it is very good indeed - but I just wanted to add that it has this really long-standing appeal unlike the vast majority of games. I don't know what exactly it is about it, but everything works so well *as a package* that it's really engrossing. The theme, the music, the decision making, the difficult (but mostly fair) gameplay, how the run develops in terms of equipment / perks / companions... Everything individualls is well-designed but it really comes together to make a super immersive experience imo.\n\nSo yeah. Just buy it. It's really great.",
